WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:49.111
DEAR X

2
00:00:49.736 --> 00:00:51.822
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES, AND EVENTS
IN THIS WORK ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:51.905 --> 00:00:53.532
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

4
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.928
- Thank you.
- Be careful.

5
00:01:15.012 --> 00:01:16.263
I will. Thank you.

6
00:01:19.474 --> 00:01:20.893
Are you all right, Mr. Choi?

7
00:01:20.976 --> 00:01:23.645
Did you really ditch the shop
to go after that thief?

8
00:01:24.146 --> 00:01:25.147
That was so brave.

9
00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.857
Why do you keep going after
those guys?

10
00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.860
- I'm fine. It was nothing.
- You should just become a cop.

11
00:01:29.943 --> 00:01:31.111
Don't be so dramatic.

12
00:01:31.195 --> 00:01:32.321
Go. I'm fine.

13
00:01:40.621 --> 00:01:43.207
BASEBALL PRODIGY CHOI JUNG HO RETIRES
AFTER A STRING OF SETBACKS

14
00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:46.043
FORMER BATTING TITLE CONTENDER
ANNOUNCES RETIREMENT

15
00:01:48.086 --> 00:01:49.630
I sometimes look back

16
00:01:50.631 --> 00:01:53.300
on those moments just before
she opened the gates of hell.

17
00:01:56.762 --> 00:02:02.142
Was Ah Jin's encounter with that man
just a coincidence?

18
00:02:03.018 --> 00:02:05.771
Or was it fate?

19
00:02:07.356 --> 00:02:08.982
- I'll see you next week.
- Take care.

20
00:02:10.859 --> 00:02:12.402
I start work next week.

21
00:02:12.986 --> 00:02:16.031
Isn't it a little too soon
to start a part-time job?

22
00:02:16.365 --> 00:02:18.700
I just want to clear my head
for a while.

23
00:02:23.038 --> 00:02:26.750
I found you a place.
Here's the address and the door code.

24
00:02:28.585 --> 00:02:32.506
It's too far from my school,
so I'll be staying with a friend.

25
00:02:32.589 --> 00:02:35.342
- The place is empty, so you can...
- No.

26
00:02:37.261 --> 00:02:38.637
I'm going back to my place.

27
00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.931
But he knows where you live.

28
00:02:41.014 --> 00:02:43.892
He'll come looking for you again
and ask for money.

29
00:02:43.976 --> 00:02:45.852
I'm going to give him the money.

30
00:02:46.311 --> 00:02:50.691
If I pay him regularly,
he won't beat me up.

31
00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:54.027
That's the best I can do.

32
00:03:02.411 --> 00:03:03.829
Bye.

33
00:03:03.912 --> 00:03:05.330
You're moving out?

34
00:03:07.374 --> 00:03:08.792
Why are you doing all this for her?

35
00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:10.127
Get a grip, Jun Seo.

36
00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.754
She's not part of your life anymore.

37
00:03:12.838 --> 00:03:15.048
You're the one who did this.

38
00:03:16.216 --> 00:03:18.844
You're the reason I can't let her go.

39
00:03:19.136 --> 00:03:20.554
What did I do?

40
00:03:20.637 --> 00:03:22.222
When her dad tried to do
those awful things

41
00:03:22.306 --> 00:03:23.557
you went along with it.

42
00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.142
After he went to prison

43
00:03:25.225 --> 00:03:28.228
you threw her out on the streets
in the middle of winter.

44
00:03:28.812 --> 00:03:30.439
You did that.

45
00:03:32.232 --> 00:03:35.819
I did what I had to do.
I had to raise you.

46
00:03:35.902 --> 00:03:37.863
I was trying to take care of you.

47
00:03:42.576 --> 00:03:43.910
Stop making excuses.

48
00:03:44.369 --> 00:03:47.331
You were just another abuser to her.

49
00:03:48.457 --> 00:03:50.917
Jun Seo, don't do this to me.

50
00:03:52.461 --> 00:03:53.545
Jun Seo.

51
00:03:54.546 --> 00:03:57.382
Jun Seo, I can't live without you!

52
00:03:59.092 --> 00:04:00.177
Jun Seo.

53
00:04:00.677 --> 00:04:02.095
This is all because of her.

54
00:04:02.888 --> 00:04:04.181
That devil.

55
00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:10.562
EPISODE 3: BREAKING THE SHACKLES

56
00:04:10.854 --> 00:04:12.022
We begin with our top story.

57
00:04:12.105 --> 00:04:13.857
Random killings are on the rise

58
00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:17.027
alongside a recent wave
of stalking-related crimes.

59
00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:18.904
In Nojeong-dong,
a string of murder victims

60
00:04:18.987 --> 00:04:24.993
were all found to have suffered
ongoing stalking before their deaths.

61
00:04:25.494 --> 00:04:26.703
Now for the weekend forecast.

62
00:04:26.787 --> 00:04:29.748
Most regions will see daytime highs
approaching 30 degrees

63
00:04:29.831 --> 00:04:31.375
as the heat continues
through the week.

64
00:04:44.971 --> 00:04:47.349
If you've finished, turn it in,
and you're free to go.

65
00:04:47.432 --> 00:04:48.975
- Okay.
- Okay.

66
00:04:56.149 --> 00:04:58.193
Did you see that girl at the cafe?

67
00:04:58.276 --> 00:04:59.986
- Yes, I saw her.
- She's gorgeous.

68
00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.947
I know, right? She's a knockout.

69
00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.032
- Do you want to go see her?
- Do you?

70
00:05:04.116 --> 00:05:05.450
- Are you down?
- Let's go.

71
00:05:08.412 --> 00:05:09.621
Enjoy your drinks.

72
00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.999
Excuse me. Do you have a boyfriend?

73
00:05:13.875 --> 00:05:14.876
Yes, I do.

74
00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.378
How about trading him for this guy?

75
00:05:16.461 --> 00:05:18.839
- He's good-looking and he's tall.
- Stop it.

76
00:05:18.922 --> 00:05:22.342
- Stand up. He's almost 190cm.
- Dude, what's wrong with you?

77
00:05:24.344 --> 00:05:28.390
I'm really sorry,
but my boyfriend's better-looking.

78
00:05:29.015 --> 00:05:30.058
I see.

79
00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:32.185
Okay.

80
00:05:34.062 --> 00:05:37.065
Thank you.
Let me know if you need anything.

81
00:05:37.149 --> 00:05:38.150
Sure.

82
00:05:43.113 --> 00:05:45.157
How many times
have you been hit on today?

83
00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.741
All the customers are guys.

84
00:05:47.409 --> 00:05:48.743
"Do you have a boyfriend?"

85
00:05:49.578 --> 00:05:50.579
Oh, right.

86
00:05:51.746 --> 00:05:53.415
Your photos are on social media.

87
00:05:54.416 --> 00:05:56.042
They're all over the internet.

88
00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.771
SHE'S LITERALLY FLAWLESS
I'M SO JEALOUS

89
00:06:16.855 --> 00:06:18.440
SHE'D OUTSHINE LE NA IF SHE DEBUTED

90
00:06:18.523 --> 00:06:20.108
WHY ISN'T SHE A CELEBRITY ALREADY?

91
00:06:20.192 --> 00:06:21.276
SHE'S GORGEOUS

92
00:06:28.325 --> 00:06:29.576
Do you remember her?

93
00:06:31.036 --> 00:06:33.246
Wait, isn't she the one
who turned us down

94
00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.832
when we tried to scout her
a few years ago?

95
00:06:35.916 --> 00:06:36.917
That's right.

96
00:06:37.626 --> 00:06:38.960
Here she is again.

97
00:06:39.044 --> 00:06:41.004
It looks like
she's not with an agency yet.

98
00:06:41.379 --> 00:06:43.632
Check again, just in case.

99
00:06:44.883 --> 00:06:47.385
Aren't you worried about your photos
spreading online?

100
00:06:48.428 --> 00:06:50.180
Should I ask them to take them down?

101
00:06:50.847 --> 00:06:53.892
Just leave it.
It's good publicity for the cafe.

102
00:06:54.601 --> 00:06:57.854
You're really pretty,
and you've got a great attitude.

103
00:06:58.563 --> 00:07:00.232
No wonder Mr. Choi likes you.

104
00:07:05.403 --> 00:07:07.989
By the way,
what is he always watching?

105
00:07:09.824 --> 00:07:11.076
You don't know?

106
00:07:11.451 --> 00:07:14.246
He was the legendary .400 hitter
and home run king.

107
00:07:14.329 --> 00:07:17.582
One swing and it was over.
It was an automatic home run.

108
00:07:18.375 --> 00:07:20.001
That's right.

109
00:07:20.085 --> 00:07:21.753
"One swing and it was over"?

110
00:07:21.836 --> 00:07:22.837
Yes.

111
00:07:23.338 --> 00:07:25.090
He was huge back then.

112
00:07:25.924 --> 00:07:27.300
What's he doing here, then?

113
00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:32.055
Kwak Eun Hyeok
went for a reckless slide

114
00:07:32.138 --> 00:07:34.182
and Mr. Choi broke his wrist
trying to tag him out.

115
00:07:34.266 --> 00:07:35.976
Three surgeries
and a year of rehab later

116
00:07:36.059 --> 00:07:37.352
he still couldn't make a comeback.

117
00:07:37.435 --> 00:07:38.645
That was the end of his career.

118
00:07:41.147 --> 00:07:45.151
He ended Mr. Choi's career,
but everyone still cheered for him.

119
00:07:47.821 --> 00:07:50.657
If I were him,
I wouldn't be able to watch baseball.

120
00:07:51.157 --> 00:07:52.284
You'd think so, right?

121
00:07:52.909 --> 00:07:55.537
Proud of you, my friend. Good job.

122
00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.873
He roots for the guy who ruined
his career and calls him a friend.

123
00:08:00.208 --> 00:08:02.002
Who knows what he's thinking?

124
00:08:04.796 --> 00:08:05.839
Welcome.

125
00:08:05.922 --> 00:08:07.549
- Hello, sir.
- Hello.

126
00:08:08.758 --> 00:08:11.094
- I come bearing good news.
- Hello.

127
00:08:14.389 --> 00:08:15.724
Who's that?

128
00:08:15.807 --> 00:08:18.476
He's Im Seung Yong, CEO of PB Agency.

129
00:08:19.853 --> 00:08:21.605
Just between us

130
00:08:22.355 --> 00:08:24.274
Mr. Choi might be signing
a new contract.

131
00:08:26.443 --> 00:08:28.695
I really hope he makes a comeback.

132
00:08:34.993 --> 00:08:36.828
- You came a long way.
- Thank you.

133
00:08:37.454 --> 00:08:39.414
He's a good man through and through.

134
00:08:41.708 --> 00:08:43.543
Why do you think

135
00:08:43.627 --> 00:08:47.297
I met someone like him
at this point in my life?

136
00:08:49.966 --> 00:08:52.260
Maybe he's your guardian spirit.

137
00:08:55.013 --> 00:08:57.390
- My guardian spirit?
- Yes.

138
00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.312
Isn't it better to believe
guardian spirits exist?

139
00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.817
If you think they're giving you
these trials for a greater purpose

140
00:09:09.611 --> 00:09:11.196
it makes life a little easier.

141
00:09:13.365 --> 00:09:17.827
If they really exist, like you said,
I wonder what their intention is.

142
00:09:25.043 --> 00:09:26.544
Hello, this is Xanadu Coffee.

143
00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.508
Did the girl working there
finish her shift?

144
00:09:32.592 --> 00:09:33.677
Who's calling?

145
00:09:34.386 --> 00:09:35.470
None of your business.

146
00:09:36.554 --> 00:09:38.807
Can I get her number?

147
00:09:40.558 --> 00:09:41.768
Excuse me.

148
00:09:41.851 --> 00:09:44.104
You need to tell me
who you are first.

149
00:09:45.021 --> 00:09:47.357
Also, I can't just give out
personal information...

150
00:09:51.945 --> 00:09:54.656
Damn, what a lunatic.

151
00:09:54.739 --> 00:09:55.740
Who was that?

152
00:09:56.116 --> 00:09:58.827
Just another guy
asking for Ah Jin's number.

153
00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:02.622
At least be polite
if you're going to ask.

154
00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.375
Ah Jin.

155
00:10:05.458 --> 00:10:08.086
Yoo Sik and I
will throw that out later.

156
00:10:08.169 --> 00:10:10.630
You should go home.
It's getting late.

157
00:10:10.714 --> 00:10:12.257
It's okay. I can do it.

158
00:10:12.882 --> 00:10:14.509
What if you miss the last bus?

159
00:10:15.593 --> 00:10:17.220
Sir, we're closed.

160
00:10:18.346 --> 00:10:19.556
We're closed for the day.

161
00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.393
But your sign is still lit.

162
00:10:23.476 --> 00:10:26.896
Sorry. Please come back tomorrow.
We have to lock up soon.

163
00:10:30.567 --> 00:10:31.860
But I want to see her.

164
00:10:31.943 --> 00:10:32.944
Where's Ah Jin?

165
00:10:33.987 --> 00:10:35.405
- Has she gone home yet?
- Well...

166
00:10:35.488 --> 00:10:39.659
Sir, please step outside.
You can come back tomorrow.

167
00:10:39.743 --> 00:10:40.910
Why are you pushing me?

168
00:10:40.994 --> 00:10:44.205
- We have to close up now.
- Can you tell Ah Jin that...

169
00:10:44.289 --> 00:10:45.874
Sorry, sir.

170
00:10:45.957 --> 00:10:48.376
Please come again tomorrow morning.

171
00:10:49.043 --> 00:10:50.128
Sorry about that.

172
00:11:07.937 --> 00:11:09.564
Did you move out?

173
00:11:09.856 --> 00:11:12.400
I only helped since I didn't want you
living with your mother.

174
00:11:12.484 --> 00:11:14.778
Don't expect me
to keep supporting you.

175
00:11:14.861 --> 00:11:18.823
When I die,
you won't get a single penny from me.

176
00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:21.493
I understand.

177
00:11:25.371 --> 00:11:27.248
Writers barely make any money.

178
00:11:27.332 --> 00:11:30.293
How do you expect to make a living?

179
00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:35.089
You still can't kill
a single ant, can you?

180
00:11:35.173 --> 00:11:38.259
Every living creature
has a reason to live.

181
00:11:38.343 --> 00:11:41.513
You sound just like him.

182
00:11:43.556 --> 00:11:45.308
Did you just laugh?

183
00:11:47.644 --> 00:11:50.438
I was just glad to hear
I take after my dad.

184
00:11:50.939 --> 00:11:52.565
Who else would you take after?

185
00:13:13.313 --> 00:13:14.981
JUN SEO

186
00:13:37.045 --> 00:13:38.046
Ah Jin?

187
00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:39.631
Ah Jin.

188
00:13:51.517 --> 00:13:53.061
What took you so long?

189
00:13:54.604 --> 00:13:57.231
Do you know
what almost happened to me?

190
00:13:57.815 --> 00:13:59.025
Ah Jin.

191
00:14:05.406 --> 00:14:06.991
Are you okay?

192
00:14:07.075 --> 00:14:09.369
Shouldn't you see a doctor?

193
00:14:09.869 --> 00:14:10.870
Are you hurt?

194
00:14:11.329 --> 00:14:12.538
Jun Seo.

195
00:14:12.622 --> 00:14:13.623
Yes.

196
00:14:15.541 --> 00:14:18.211
How far would you go for me?

197
00:14:25.009 --> 00:14:26.052
Answer me.

198
00:14:26.928 --> 00:14:29.055
How far would you go for me?

199
00:14:29.722 --> 00:14:30.932
I'd do anything for you.

200
00:14:31.933 --> 00:14:33.726
As long as it doesn't involve
killing someone

201
00:14:34.102 --> 00:14:36.312
I'll do anything you ask me.

202
00:14:39.148 --> 00:14:41.734
So you're letting your conscience
decide where the line is?

203
00:14:43.361 --> 00:14:45.571
- That's not what I mean.
- Don't worry.

204
00:14:45.655 --> 00:14:48.199
I never expected you
to go that far in the first place.

205
00:14:52.745 --> 00:14:55.873
If you were brave enough
to kill a man for me

206
00:14:55.957 --> 00:14:58.543
I'd have asked you
to start with Baek Seon Gyu.

207
00:15:05.758 --> 00:15:08.553
You can kill anything
besides a man for me then, right?

208
00:15:17.729 --> 00:15:18.730
Help...

209
00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:20.481
Help me.

210
00:15:21.774 --> 00:15:23.276
Please.

211
00:15:26.654 --> 00:15:29.824
If you want to spare your life,
forget what happened tonight.

212
00:15:29.907 --> 00:15:33.870
If you promise
to keep your mouth shut

213
00:15:33.953 --> 00:15:35.955
I can call you an ambulance.

214
00:15:36.039 --> 00:15:37.623
I won't say a word.

215
00:15:37.707 --> 00:15:38.708
I promise.

216
00:15:39.375 --> 00:15:41.252
There's a man injured
in the second alley

217
00:15:41.335 --> 00:15:42.670
behind the Nojeong-gu townhouses.

218
00:15:42.754 --> 00:15:45.840
It looks like a random assault.
He's losing a lot of blood.

219
00:16:36.265 --> 00:16:38.893
Did you put the money
under the second flowerpot?

220
00:16:51.572 --> 00:16:52.573
Hey.

221
00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:56.619
She's easy on the eyes.

222
00:16:58.329 --> 00:17:00.248
Get me a contact.

223
00:17:00.873 --> 00:17:04.001
Put her in front of a camera
or ship her off to some island.

224
00:17:04.585 --> 00:17:06.462
Just make sure it pays top dollar.

225
00:17:10.174 --> 00:17:13.970
I might have to sell an organ
to pay off the interest.

226
00:17:14.887 --> 00:17:18.307
I'm her father.
It's the least she can do for me.

227
00:17:19.433 --> 00:17:22.019
I made that girl.
I brought her into this world.

228
00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:23.980
She belongs to me.

229
00:17:25.064 --> 00:17:27.525
I'll do whatever I want with her.
Got a problem with that?

230
00:17:29.527 --> 00:17:30.570
Ah Jin.

231
00:17:41.831 --> 00:17:43.666
What?

232
00:17:44.584 --> 00:17:47.003
Were you going to push me off
this building?

233
00:17:48.004 --> 00:17:49.797
Don't do anything stupid.

234
00:17:50.923 --> 00:17:53.968
If you kill me, you'll be ostracized.

235
00:17:54.677 --> 00:17:57.471
Your life will be over, you bitch.

236
00:18:08.065 --> 00:18:09.275
You're pathetic.

237
00:18:10.276 --> 00:18:12.778
I get you hate your old man,
but how dare you?

238
00:18:13.905 --> 00:18:15.907
I can see right through you, bitch.

239
00:18:20.828 --> 00:18:22.622
Next month, I want double the money.

240
00:19:29.563 --> 00:19:30.648
Hey.

241
00:19:31.357 --> 00:19:34.610
I'm saying this
out of old times' sake.

242
00:19:35.486 --> 00:19:37.071
Stay away from that girl.

243
00:19:37.905 --> 00:19:39.198
She's bad news.

244
00:19:40.116 --> 00:19:42.535
Don't let her ruin your life, okay?

245
00:20:02.388 --> 00:20:03.514
What did he do to you?

246
00:20:10.438 --> 00:20:11.522
Jun Seo.

247
00:20:13.107 --> 00:20:14.692
Can you hit me?

248
00:20:15.192 --> 00:20:16.193
What?

249
00:20:16.277 --> 00:20:18.029
It has to look like
a stalker attacked me.

250
00:20:19.363 --> 00:20:20.781
Just hit me a few times.

251
00:20:26.454 --> 00:20:27.830
No.

252
00:20:28.414 --> 00:20:29.749
I can't do that.

253
00:20:30.624 --> 00:20:31.751
I won't.

254
00:20:32.626 --> 00:20:33.627
You won't?

255
00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.629
I won't.

256
00:20:36.964 --> 00:20:38.549
Are you serious?

257
00:20:38.632 --> 00:20:39.884
I should ask you that.

258
00:20:39.967 --> 00:20:43.596
Are you seriously asking me
to hit you?

259
00:20:43.679 --> 00:20:45.097
It's nothing new.

260
00:20:46.849 --> 00:20:48.893
You've seen me get hit before.

261
00:20:48.976 --> 00:20:51.937
That's exactly why I can't hit you.

262
00:20:52.021 --> 00:20:56.150
It tore me apart,
and it still haunts me.

263
00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.495
Fine.

264
00:21:08.537 --> 00:21:11.332
I won't force you to do it.

265
00:21:13.626 --> 00:21:14.710
Jun Seo.

266
00:21:16.796 --> 00:21:19.715
I don't care if you get hurt

267
00:21:20.299 --> 00:21:22.802
but I don't want to be the one
who hurts you.

268
00:21:23.844 --> 00:21:25.304
I don't want to lose you.

269
00:21:27.056 --> 00:21:32.228
You know I don't treat you
like I treat everyone else.

270
00:21:42.029 --> 00:21:43.030
Ah Jin.

271
00:21:44.365 --> 00:21:46.325
Sometimes, you scare me.

272
00:21:48.369 --> 00:21:52.581
But I think it's because
you weren't loved growing up

273
00:21:53.624 --> 00:21:55.459
so I don't know what to do.

274
00:22:00.339 --> 00:22:01.632
Ah Jin.

275
00:22:05.511 --> 00:22:06.804
I'll handle this.

276
00:22:43.132 --> 00:22:44.842
Did something happen?

277
00:22:44.925 --> 00:22:45.926
Pardon?

278
00:22:47.219 --> 00:22:49.972
No, nothing happened.

279
00:22:50.055 --> 00:22:51.557
It's just a little scratch.

280
00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:53.809
You know you can tell me anything.

281
00:22:54.685 --> 00:22:56.270
Don't bottle it up.

282
00:22:58.814 --> 00:23:00.858
Believe it or not, I'm pretty strong.

283
00:23:01.734 --> 00:23:04.195
I've never lost a fight before.

284
00:23:04.278 --> 00:23:05.321
Okay?

285
00:23:08.866 --> 00:23:10.242
You don't believe me?

286
00:23:10.951 --> 00:23:12.244
I do.

287
00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:15.289
I may be the boss

288
00:23:15.372 --> 00:23:18.209
but you and Yoo Sik
are like family to me.

289
00:23:19.627 --> 00:23:24.632
So whatever it is,
go ahead and use me, okay?

290
00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:27.510
Use you?

291
00:23:30.638 --> 00:23:32.097
That's right. Whatever it is.

292
00:23:33.224 --> 00:23:35.518
But you're my boss.

293
00:23:36.644 --> 00:23:39.063
That's what bosses are for.

294
00:23:39.563 --> 00:23:43.150
Since Jun Seo has classes
late at night

295
00:23:43.234 --> 00:23:44.818
I worry about you going home alone.

296
00:23:44.902 --> 00:23:47.279
You said it's just you
and your father, right?

297
00:23:47.363 --> 00:23:50.616
Yes, but my father lives far away.

298
00:23:52.326 --> 00:23:56.163
I'd feel a lot more at ease
if your father lived close by.

299
00:23:56.914 --> 00:23:58.332
What does he do?

300
00:23:59.375 --> 00:24:01.168
He just works at a company.

301
00:24:01.252 --> 00:24:02.795
He works the night shift.

302
00:24:03.504 --> 00:24:06.382
WOMEN'S RESTROOM

303
00:24:12.846 --> 00:24:14.098
Shit.

304
00:24:43.711 --> 00:24:47.506
How much would we make
if we used an actress

305
00:24:47.590 --> 00:24:49.592
instead of planting hidden cameras?

306
00:24:50.884 --> 00:24:52.970
She's drop-dead gorgeous.

307
00:24:54.805 --> 00:24:55.889
Yeah?

308
00:24:57.850 --> 00:25:02.688
So I just need to drug her
and drop her off for a few hours?

309
00:25:05.316 --> 00:25:06.317
Shit.

310
00:25:10.821 --> 00:25:13.699
I found a hidden-camera offender.
I have proof, and I'm in pursuit.

311
00:25:33.427 --> 00:25:35.095
You little punk!

312
00:25:35.596 --> 00:25:39.183
If you hadn't called the cops
back then

313
00:25:39.266 --> 00:25:41.685
I wouldn't have gone to prison!

314
00:25:41.769 --> 00:25:46.940
My life is fucked up because of you!

315
00:25:48.359 --> 00:25:49.401
Baek Ah Jin.

316
00:25:50.402 --> 00:25:52.154
She's your daughter.

317
00:25:53.614 --> 00:25:57.993
I brought her into this world,
so I'll do what I want with her.

318
00:25:58.494 --> 00:26:00.704
Stay out of it.

319
00:26:13.926 --> 00:26:20.808
She belongs to me
until the day she dies, you bastard.

320
00:26:20.891 --> 00:26:23.268
Die!

321
00:27:16.447 --> 00:27:17.740
Police! Step away!

322
00:27:20.367 --> 00:27:21.994
You're under arrest for assault.

323
00:27:26.832 --> 00:27:27.833
Sir, are you okay?

324
00:27:28.667 --> 00:27:29.668
I think so.

325
00:27:33.881 --> 00:27:35.090
Can you stand?

326
00:27:38.594 --> 00:27:39.595
This way.

327
00:27:41.597 --> 00:27:45.058
YEONGDONG POLICE STATION

328
00:27:45.601 --> 00:27:47.436
So you two were step-siblings.

329
00:27:47.519 --> 00:27:51.982
After your parents split up,
you kept stalking Baek Ah Jin.

330
00:27:52.941 --> 00:27:56.779
And when her father found out,
you threatened to kill him?

331
00:27:58.238 --> 00:27:59.239
Ah Jin.

332
00:28:01.366 --> 00:28:03.660
Do you have proof
that he's been stalking you?

333
00:28:04.119 --> 00:28:05.120
Text messages, perhaps?

334
00:28:05.662 --> 00:28:09.166
A few days ago,
he was hiding at my place.

335
00:28:14.379 --> 00:28:15.631
And he did this to me.

336
00:28:19.009 --> 00:28:22.221
No, this man was the one
who did that to her.

337
00:28:22.304 --> 00:28:25.724
He collects hidden-camera footage
from restrooms and gambles illegally.

338
00:28:25.808 --> 00:28:29.645
I spoke with Detective Jin Dong Gyu
so I could hand over the evidence.

339
00:28:29.728 --> 00:28:32.815
He did reach out to us.
So do you have the evidence?

340
00:28:33.607 --> 00:28:34.942
I do.

341
00:28:37.194 --> 00:28:38.320
It's on my phone.

342
00:28:39.530 --> 00:28:40.614
Looking for this?

343
00:29:16.525 --> 00:29:18.735
Show me the evidence.

344
00:29:20.028 --> 00:29:21.530
You said it was on your phone.

345
00:29:22.781 --> 00:29:23.782
Show me.

346
00:29:24.741 --> 00:29:27.703
If you filed a false report,
the charges will be even heavier!

347
00:29:37.337 --> 00:29:39.131
I'll be coming into some money soon.

348
00:29:39.214 --> 00:29:41.967
I'll contact you,
so don't reach out to me until then.

349
00:29:42.968 --> 00:29:44.720
You're not bluffing, right?

350
00:29:45.554 --> 00:29:48.682
If I'm lying,
you can do whatever you want to me.

351
00:29:50.142 --> 00:29:53.770
You've grown up. You really have.

352
00:29:56.315 --> 00:29:57.316
Call me.

353
00:30:01.361 --> 00:30:03.238
Damn it.

354
00:30:12.205 --> 00:30:13.206
Detective.

355
00:30:15.334 --> 00:30:18.837
May I have a moment with Jun Seo?

356
00:30:19.379 --> 00:30:20.964
I'm afraid not.

357
00:30:21.048 --> 00:30:24.384
It's against protocol for the victim
and the offender to have contact.

358
00:30:24.885 --> 00:30:27.012
Before all this happened,
we were siblings.

359
00:30:27.679 --> 00:30:30.641
I only need a minute. Please.

360
00:30:39.483 --> 00:30:40.651
What are you doing?

361
00:30:42.527 --> 00:30:44.613
If we go with your plan
and pin him as a petty offender

362
00:30:44.696 --> 00:30:46.406
he'll be out in a few years.

363
00:30:46.490 --> 00:30:48.450
It won't change a thing.

364
00:30:48.909 --> 00:30:51.495
Don't be reckless.
You can't beat him.

365
00:30:54.456 --> 00:30:55.958
I said I'd handle it.

366
00:30:56.041 --> 00:30:58.794
You should've smashed his head
with that brick.

367
00:30:59.670 --> 00:31:00.879
But you hesitated.

368
00:31:02.172 --> 00:31:04.132
That's why you can't beat him.

369
00:31:04.925 --> 00:31:06.218
So stay out of it.

370
00:31:09.763 --> 00:31:11.932
Ah Jin.

371
00:31:12.599 --> 00:31:13.600
Ah Jin.

372
00:31:29.074 --> 00:31:30.909
Mr. Choi was
a professional athlete, right?

373
00:31:30.993 --> 00:31:33.286
One swing and it was over.
It was an automatic home run.

374
00:31:33.370 --> 00:31:35.038
"One swing and it was over"?

375
00:31:35.122 --> 00:31:36.665
Don't do anything stupid.

376
00:31:37.332 --> 00:31:40.585
If you kill me, you'll be ostracized.

377
00:31:40.919 --> 00:31:44.256
You and Yoo Sik
are like family to me.

378
00:31:45.340 --> 00:31:49.428
Whatever it is,
go ahead and use me, okay?

379
00:32:11.616 --> 00:32:13.493
- Hey, Ah Jin.
- Good morning.

380
00:32:14.411 --> 00:32:15.787
What happened to your face?

381
00:32:15.871 --> 00:32:17.706
I fell.

382
00:32:18.498 --> 00:32:21.752
You expect me to believe that?
That's not from a fall.

383
00:32:21.835 --> 00:32:23.170
I'm okay.

384
00:32:24.212 --> 00:32:27.591
Tell me the truth.
Who did this to you?

385
00:32:28.383 --> 00:32:30.010
And that scratch on your neck.

386
00:32:30.093 --> 00:32:32.179
Tell me what really happened.

387
00:32:32.262 --> 00:32:33.388
Well...

388
00:32:34.765 --> 00:32:36.516
The thing is...

389
00:32:37.225 --> 00:32:40.437
I didn't say anything
because I didn't want you to worry.

390
00:32:40.520 --> 00:32:45.525
But some guy has been following me
for a few days now.

391
00:32:47.152 --> 00:32:49.863
We had a bit of a scuffle last night.

392
00:32:49.946 --> 00:32:51.156
Did you call the police?

393
00:32:51.615 --> 00:32:56.328
They said, unless he assaults me
or commits a crime

394
00:32:56.912 --> 00:32:59.581
there's not much they can do
if the stalker denies it.

395
00:33:02.167 --> 00:33:05.796
Jun Seo is staying with his grandpa
for a few days

396
00:33:05.879 --> 00:33:07.589
so I am a little worried.

397
00:33:13.512 --> 00:33:14.596
This won't do.

398
00:33:14.679 --> 00:33:16.181
- Yoo Sik.
- Yes?

399
00:33:16.264 --> 00:33:18.725
- Close up by yourself for now.
- What?

400
00:33:18.809 --> 00:33:20.685
I'll take her home
for the time being.

401
00:33:21.311 --> 00:33:23.647
- But...
- Thank you, Mr. Choi.

402
00:33:30.570 --> 00:33:31.571
Take it.

403
00:33:32.739 --> 00:33:33.824
What's this?

404
00:33:34.574 --> 00:33:38.161
It's pepper spray. You might need it.

405
00:33:40.205 --> 00:33:43.125
Thank you for looking out for me.

406
00:33:45.335 --> 00:33:47.379
I hope you never have to use it.

407
00:33:49.464 --> 00:33:51.716
Do you ever regret it?

408
00:33:52.509 --> 00:33:54.886
Regret what?

409
00:33:57.347 --> 00:34:00.225
Helping someone
when it isn't really your problem.

410
00:34:01.518 --> 00:34:04.396
Sacrificing yourself for no gain.

411
00:34:05.272 --> 00:34:10.068
Forgiving and rooting for the friend
who ruined your career.

412
00:34:11.695 --> 00:34:14.114
I don't know.

413
00:34:14.865 --> 00:34:15.949
Do I regret it?

414
00:34:18.326 --> 00:34:19.411
Not really.

415
00:34:20.662 --> 00:34:22.956
I'm not the type to dwell on regrets.

416
00:34:24.332 --> 00:34:25.542
It's just how I am.

417
00:34:29.796 --> 00:34:33.800
What if it backfires
and you end up hurting yourself?

418
00:34:35.343 --> 00:34:37.971
I just follow my conscience.

419
00:34:38.889 --> 00:34:41.683
I can't get anything done
when my conscience feels heavy.

420
00:34:42.392 --> 00:34:47.147
Even if I end up getting hurt,
if that's the result of my choice

421
00:34:47.731 --> 00:34:49.149
then so be it.

422
00:34:54.863 --> 00:34:57.282
I hope you never change.

423
00:34:58.074 --> 00:35:00.327
It's better for you that way.

424
00:35:02.787 --> 00:35:06.499
You're a good person.

425
00:35:10.754 --> 00:35:12.464
Hey, kiddo.

426
00:35:13.506 --> 00:35:15.133
He's a good adult.

427
00:35:16.384 --> 00:35:19.346
He's driven by justice
and willing to help others.

428
00:35:19.429 --> 00:35:20.722
Is that a compliment?

429
00:35:20.805 --> 00:35:24.142
He's the kind of adult
I need right now.

430
00:35:38.865 --> 00:35:40.075
Thank you.

431
00:35:40.617 --> 00:35:42.118
You live here alone?

432
00:35:47.499 --> 00:35:49.292
I'll get you a studio near the cafe.

433
00:35:50.001 --> 00:35:51.211
You should move.

434
00:35:52.963 --> 00:35:54.965
You can't live here by yourself.

435
00:35:56.800 --> 00:36:01.054
The rent might be higher,
but safety comes first.

436
00:36:01.429 --> 00:36:02.597
That's a bit...

437
00:36:03.515 --> 00:36:06.685
You don't need to worry
about the deposit.

438
00:36:08.270 --> 00:36:10.647
Think of it as an advance
on your severance.

439
00:36:11.773 --> 00:36:15.944
I appreciate your concern.
I'll think it over.

440
00:36:17.654 --> 00:36:18.655
Okay.

441
00:36:19.614 --> 00:36:20.699
Get home safely.

442
00:36:32.752 --> 00:36:34.462
What's wrong? What is it?

443
00:36:35.380 --> 00:36:36.423
Shoot.

444
00:36:37.757 --> 00:36:39.342
What kind of psycho...

445
00:36:42.304 --> 00:36:43.513
What's that?

446
00:36:43.930 --> 00:36:45.390
YOU'RE NEXT

447
00:36:45.473 --> 00:36:46.516
"You're next"?

448
00:36:55.608 --> 00:36:56.651
Hey!

449
00:36:57.694 --> 00:36:59.738
Ah Jin, go inside and lock the door.

450
00:37:27.349 --> 00:37:28.933
Stop right there!

451
00:37:29.851 --> 00:37:30.935
Stop!

452
00:37:49.412 --> 00:37:51.790
What are you doing out here?

453
00:37:51.873 --> 00:37:53.666
I told you to go inside
and lock the door.

454
00:37:54.167 --> 00:37:57.796
You went after the stalker,
so I couldn't just sit still.

455
00:37:58.755 --> 00:37:59.756
Are you okay?

456
00:38:00.048 --> 00:38:01.591
I'm fine.

457
00:38:04.135 --> 00:38:05.637
But I lost him.

458
00:38:06.805 --> 00:38:08.681
It's getting late.
You should go home.

459
00:38:08.765 --> 00:38:11.643
I can't leave you here alone.

460
00:38:13.144 --> 00:38:15.397
Let me at least take you
to a sauna or...

461
00:38:15.480 --> 00:38:16.523
I'm okay.

462
00:38:16.606 --> 00:38:19.609
I already asked a friend
to come over.

463
00:38:20.485 --> 00:38:21.694
Don't worry.

464
00:38:22.362 --> 00:38:24.656
You should go. I'll head in too.

465
00:38:25.698 --> 00:38:26.699
All right.

466
00:39:19.878 --> 00:39:21.421
I left a bat by your door.

467
00:39:21.504 --> 00:39:23.756
It's better to be safe than sorry.

468
00:39:24.174 --> 00:39:27.218
Everything has its use.

469
00:39:28.344 --> 00:39:34.601
Even small things, if used right,
can turn into an opportunity.

470
00:39:35.935 --> 00:39:37.770
How about some beer
and fried chicken?

471
00:39:37.854 --> 00:39:39.689
- I'm too full.
- What do you say?

472
00:39:39.772 --> 00:39:40.857
Come on, let's go.

473
00:39:43.526 --> 00:39:44.819
I need to buy cigarettes.

474
00:39:46.738 --> 00:39:48.031
Where are you going?

475
00:39:48.114 --> 00:39:50.325
Hey, it's Ah Jin.

476
00:40:02.128 --> 00:40:03.671
Where do you think you're going?

477
00:40:03.755 --> 00:40:05.965
- Wait, I know her.
- Let's hit the karaoke.

478
00:40:06.466 --> 00:40:08.259
- I know her. Get off me.
- Let's go.

479
00:40:09.385 --> 00:40:10.720
Come on.

480
00:40:11.346 --> 00:40:13.097
- What are you doing?
- I'm not going home.

481
00:40:13.932 --> 00:40:15.016
Hurry up.

482
00:40:15.099 --> 00:40:17.644
Where's Ah Jin?
Has she gone home yet?

483
00:40:17.727 --> 00:40:20.313
- Let's go!
- What's the holdup?

484
00:40:20.396 --> 00:40:22.440
- Hurry up.
- I'm coming.

485
00:40:22.524 --> 00:40:23.525
Let's go.

486
00:40:23.608 --> 00:40:25.818
- What are you looking at?
- Hurry up.

487
00:41:15.034 --> 00:41:18.788
I'll give you the money.
Be at my place by 8 p.m.

488
00:41:18.871 --> 00:41:22.917
People only come to their senses
when they're scared.

489
00:41:28.798 --> 00:41:32.969
"Fortune may turn into misfortune.
Tread carefully."

490
00:41:34.095 --> 00:41:36.180
What the hell? How annoying.

491
00:41:47.817 --> 00:41:48.818
Morning.

492
00:41:50.028 --> 00:41:52.447
Ah Jin, someone's looking for you.

493
00:41:55.325 --> 00:41:56.409
You know her?

494
00:42:05.543 --> 00:42:06.544
Hello.

495
00:42:08.838 --> 00:42:12.634
Ah Jin, are you sure
you don't want to give acting a try?

496
00:42:13.134 --> 00:42:14.594
Why me?

497
00:42:15.928 --> 00:42:18.640
Aren't there tons of people
desperate to be actors?

498
00:42:18.723 --> 00:42:21.726
You were born with something
others don't have.

499
00:42:22.977 --> 00:42:24.187
Be honest with me.

500
00:42:25.188 --> 00:42:27.315
You have thought about it,
haven't you?

501
00:42:27.398 --> 00:42:31.194
You're right. You've been on my mind.

502
00:42:33.237 --> 00:42:35.990
But I can't right now.
I have to take care of something.

503
00:42:36.074 --> 00:42:38.493
Can I ask you what that is?

504
00:42:40.620 --> 00:42:42.205
It's a family matter.

505
00:42:42.580 --> 00:42:46.793
If you're looking after
a sick family member, we can help.

506
00:42:47.960 --> 00:42:50.380
No, it's something
I have to do myself.

507
00:42:51.839 --> 00:42:52.840
Oh, well.

508
00:42:54.926 --> 00:42:56.761
That's a shame.

509
00:42:57.553 --> 00:43:00.264
But you seem set on your decision.

510
00:43:01.015 --> 00:43:02.809
If you ever change your mind

511
00:43:02.892 --> 00:43:05.436
promise you'll work with me,
not anyone else.

512
00:43:06.270 --> 00:43:09.357
I'll treat you better
than any other agency.

513
00:43:10.233 --> 00:43:11.234
I appreciate it.

514
00:43:11.818 --> 00:43:14.654
All right, then. I'll see you around.

515
00:43:21.953 --> 00:43:23.579
- Thank you for coming.
- Goodbye.

516
00:43:27.333 --> 00:43:29.043
Should I get your autograph now?

517
00:43:30.336 --> 00:43:32.255
I turned it down.

518
00:43:32.338 --> 00:43:33.381
Why?

519
00:43:33.464 --> 00:43:35.842
You'll be famous and rich.
What's not to like?

520
00:43:36.509 --> 00:43:38.344
I just like the way it is now.

521
00:43:40.012 --> 00:43:42.140
Jun Seo better watch out.

522
00:43:43.141 --> 00:43:45.226
His girlfriend might become
a superstar.

523
00:43:45.309 --> 00:43:48.229
Girlfriend? I'm not his girlfriend.

524
00:43:50.189 --> 00:43:52.984
You're not? Then what's the deal?

525
00:43:57.238 --> 00:43:58.406
Still no guardian?

526
00:44:05.246 --> 00:44:07.415
Nothing happened last night, right?

527
00:44:09.917 --> 00:44:13.337
I was too scared,
so I spent the night at my friend's.

528
00:44:14.547 --> 00:44:18.634
But when I got home this morning,
my place was a mess.

529
00:44:18.718 --> 00:44:20.595
I think someone broke in.

530
00:44:26.267 --> 00:44:28.770
Does Jun Seo know about this?

531
00:44:29.854 --> 00:44:32.607
I didn't want him to worry,
so I didn't tell him.

532
00:44:33.357 --> 00:44:35.276
I'll tell him
when he gets back tomorrow.

533
00:44:35.359 --> 00:44:36.861
I'm also thinking of moving.

534
00:44:37.361 --> 00:44:39.614
- What about tonight?
- Tonight?

535
00:44:40.656 --> 00:44:42.325
I'll have to manage.

536
00:44:47.955 --> 00:44:48.956
Then...

537
00:44:50.458 --> 00:44:53.544
Let's do this.
Sleep at my place tonight.

538
00:44:55.421 --> 00:44:57.548
I'll sleep somewhere else.

539
00:44:58.716 --> 00:45:01.260
I can stay at my parents' house.

540
00:45:02.637 --> 00:45:04.722
No, it's okay.

541
00:45:06.015 --> 00:45:10.812
You don't seem to get it.
This could be really dangerous.

542
00:45:12.313 --> 00:45:15.525
Don't you have a meeting
with your agent tonight?

543
00:45:15.608 --> 00:45:16.609
I do.

544
00:45:16.692 --> 00:45:19.028
I'll go to my parents'
after the meeting.

545
00:45:20.112 --> 00:45:22.824
So stay at my place tonight.

546
00:45:24.992 --> 00:45:28.037
Jun Seo will be back tomorrow,
so just until then.

547
00:45:28.704 --> 00:45:33.292
You should also reconsider moving
to a studio that's near the cafe.

548
00:45:33.709 --> 00:45:35.419
I will, Mr. Choi.

549
00:45:46.222 --> 00:45:48.224
It's raining cats and dogs out there.

550
00:45:49.141 --> 00:45:51.853
In movies, bad things happen
when it rains like this.

551
00:45:52.436 --> 00:45:54.605
You watch too many movies.

552
00:46:02.446 --> 00:46:04.198
What's wrong?

553
00:46:04.699 --> 00:46:05.700
Nothing.

554
00:46:06.659 --> 00:46:07.910
What is it?

555
00:46:12.039 --> 00:46:15.209
I think I saw the stalker
in the beanie last night.

556
00:46:16.002 --> 00:46:17.003
Where?

557
00:46:18.504 --> 00:46:19.672
At a convenience store.

558
00:46:20.631 --> 00:46:22.800
And he was with...

559
00:46:24.886 --> 00:46:26.053
Who was he with?

560
00:46:41.360 --> 00:46:42.361
What happened?

561
00:46:42.987 --> 00:46:45.740
I'm sorry.
I didn't sleep so well last night.

562
00:46:48.659 --> 00:46:50.411
Wait here. I'll grab some ointment.

563
00:46:58.711 --> 00:47:00.880
Didn't you say you had
a memorial service to get to?

564
00:47:01.589 --> 00:47:03.466
Shouldn't you be on your way?

565
00:47:04.425 --> 00:47:06.510
You're right. I should.

566
00:47:50.846 --> 00:47:52.056
To Gudeok-dong?

567
00:47:52.848 --> 00:47:53.849
Get in.

568
00:47:55.685 --> 00:47:57.645
It's Building A, Unit 504.

569
00:47:57.728 --> 00:48:00.398
I'll text you the door code.
Just punch that in and go inside.

570
00:48:00.690 --> 00:48:02.650
Thank you.
Good luck with your meeting.

571
00:48:02.733 --> 00:48:04.360
Text me if you need anything.

572
00:48:04.443 --> 00:48:05.444
Okay.

573
00:48:23.379 --> 00:48:24.714
Sir.

574
00:48:24.797 --> 00:48:28.551
Could you take me to 13 Nojeong-dong
instead of Gudeok-dong?

575
00:48:39.812 --> 00:48:44.025
Mr. Choi, I need to stop by my place
to grab a few things.

576
00:48:49.739 --> 00:48:52.867
What? Right now?
Are you going to be okay?

577
00:48:52.950 --> 00:48:54.618
I would have gone with you, then.

578
00:49:00.624 --> 00:49:01.917
It'll only take a minute.

579
00:49:03.002 --> 00:49:05.504
I just need to grab my wallet and ID.

580
00:49:09.383 --> 00:49:12.053
Ask the driver to wait
in front of your place.

581
00:49:12.845 --> 00:49:14.597
Call me if anything happens.

582
00:49:47.880 --> 00:49:49.715
I thought you ran off.

583
00:49:49.799 --> 00:49:53.260
You told me to be here at this time.
What took you so long?

584
00:49:54.970 --> 00:49:57.515
You must be mad I kept you waiting.

585
00:49:58.849 --> 00:50:00.810
You weren't the only one
who had to wait.

586
00:50:00.893 --> 00:50:03.270
I've also been waiting
for this moment.

587
00:50:04.355 --> 00:50:06.273
Cut the crap and give me the money.

588
00:50:06.649 --> 00:50:08.776
I'll give you the money.

589
00:50:11.195 --> 00:50:12.738
But can you put this on first?

590
00:50:14.073 --> 00:50:15.199
What's this?

591
00:50:15.282 --> 00:50:16.492
It's a gift.

592
00:50:18.327 --> 00:50:20.663
Ever since I was little

593
00:50:22.123 --> 00:50:23.415
I used to wonder

594
00:50:24.208 --> 00:50:28.629
how nice it'd be if we got along
and had a good relationship.

595
00:50:31.799 --> 00:50:36.303
Now that I'm earning money,
I wanted to get you something nice.

596
00:50:37.972 --> 00:50:40.266
I'll give you the money,
so put this on.

597
00:50:40.349 --> 00:50:41.725
It's your birthday gift, Dad.

598
00:50:42.893 --> 00:50:44.103
You've lost your mind.

599
00:50:44.895 --> 00:50:46.355
Calling me "Dad"?

600
00:50:47.189 --> 00:50:48.983
What are you up to?

601
00:50:49.066 --> 00:50:50.818
Just try it on.

602
00:50:50.901 --> 00:50:53.320
It's not that difficult.

603
00:50:54.029 --> 00:50:56.782
Just put it on for me.

604
00:50:57.283 --> 00:50:59.451
If you do that,
I'll give you the money.

605
00:51:06.792 --> 00:51:08.127
Did you put poison on this?

606
00:51:08.836 --> 00:51:10.004
I'll put it on for you.

607
00:51:19.555 --> 00:51:20.556
Dad.

608
00:51:26.437 --> 00:51:27.897
You look so good.

609
00:51:30.524 --> 00:51:31.942
It really suits you.

610
00:51:47.541 --> 00:51:50.836
All right. I put it on.
Now, give me the money.

611
00:52:09.813 --> 00:52:11.190
You've changed.

612
00:52:11.523 --> 00:52:14.693
You used to be so spiteful.
Maybe you're finally growing up.

613
00:52:16.362 --> 00:52:18.489
You need to toughen up.

614
00:52:19.490 --> 00:52:21.992
You have to be ruthless to survive.

615
00:52:22.076 --> 00:52:24.286
It's a cruel world out there.

616
00:52:24.828 --> 00:52:28.165
It can turn on you in a second.

617
00:53:02.199 --> 00:53:03.993
You crazy bitch.

618
00:53:11.250 --> 00:53:14.128
Did you actually think
I'd give you the money?

619
00:53:14.211 --> 00:53:16.922
You'll just take the money and leave.

620
00:53:20.801 --> 00:53:25.848
But you know what?
I need you today, Dad.

621
00:53:26.807 --> 00:53:29.893
Tell me. Do you want to kill me now?

622
00:53:33.939 --> 00:53:36.942
If that's what you want,
I'll kill you.

623
00:53:37.026 --> 00:53:38.235
You little...

624
00:53:40.404 --> 00:53:41.697
Come here.

625
00:53:47.953 --> 00:53:49.580
Did you have fun?

626
00:53:50.539 --> 00:53:52.499
You should smile. This is fun, right?

627
00:53:53.125 --> 00:53:54.293
Stand up.

628
00:53:56.128 --> 00:53:58.464
- Hey, Ah Jin.
- I'm calling the police!

629
00:53:58.547 --> 00:54:00.424
Go ahead. Call them.

630
00:54:00.507 --> 00:54:02.885
- Help!
- Hello? Ah Jin?

631
00:54:03.969 --> 00:54:04.970
Ah Jin...

632
00:54:29.661 --> 00:54:32.581
The call cannot be connected.
Please leave a message...

633
00:54:33.082 --> 00:54:35.334
YEONGDONG POLICE STATION

634
00:54:37.252 --> 00:54:39.296
CALLING AH JIN

635
00:54:48.931 --> 00:54:50.015
Get over here.

636
00:54:51.058 --> 00:54:52.643
MR. CHOI

637
00:54:53.143 --> 00:54:54.144
Shit.

638
00:55:03.153 --> 00:55:06.073
- This is the police.
- There's been a break-in.

639
00:55:06.698 --> 00:55:07.908
What's the address?

640
00:55:07.991 --> 00:55:09.201
Nojeong-dong.

641
00:55:09.284 --> 00:55:10.661
Are you near Nojeong Station?

642
00:55:11.120 --> 00:55:13.414
No, not near the station.

643
00:55:13.997 --> 00:55:15.666
Could you give me the exact address?

644
00:55:16.125 --> 00:55:19.086
I don't know the exact address.

645
00:55:26.635 --> 00:55:28.178
I have to endure this.

646
00:55:28.262 --> 00:55:30.889
It takes ten minutes
to get here from the cafe.

647
00:55:32.891 --> 00:55:34.601
I just need to hold on
for ten minutes.

648
00:55:39.189 --> 00:55:40.190
Hey.

649
00:55:40.899 --> 00:55:43.277
Hey...hey!

650
00:55:46.864 --> 00:55:48.532
I won't let you die so easily.

651
00:55:49.283 --> 00:55:51.076
I don't have the money in my hands.

652
00:55:51.160 --> 00:55:53.162
Why did you have to piss me off?

653
00:55:57.583 --> 00:55:58.876
Damn it.

654
00:56:07.843 --> 00:56:11.096
What? Do you want some more of this?

655
00:56:14.975 --> 00:56:16.602
I'll give you the money!

656
00:56:37.289 --> 00:56:38.457
Shit.

657
00:56:53.305 --> 00:56:54.306
Shit.

658
00:56:57.809 --> 00:56:58.894
Damn it!

659
00:57:06.693 --> 00:57:07.694
Fuck.

660
00:57:08.654 --> 00:57:10.739
Fucking bitch!

661
00:57:31.927 --> 00:57:35.013
Do I have to break your hand
for you to be a good girl?

662
00:58:32.237 --> 00:58:35.741
You were pretty
even when you were a baby.

663
00:58:42.039 --> 00:58:43.123
Cry.

664
00:58:45.208 --> 00:58:46.585
Wah.

665
00:58:47.878 --> 00:58:48.879
Come on.

666
00:58:51.798 --> 00:58:53.592
Cry for me.

667
00:58:58.430 --> 00:58:59.931
That's it.

668
00:59:09.149 --> 00:59:10.525
That's what I'm talking about!

669
00:59:10.609 --> 00:59:14.821
Ah Jin wagered her life
in a gamble with God.

670
00:59:33.799 --> 00:59:35.676
You crazy bastard! Get off her!

671
00:59:41.056 --> 00:59:43.892
Ah Jin, are you okay?

672
00:59:45.852 --> 00:59:47.062
Fuck you!

673
00:59:56.071 --> 00:59:58.532
She's young enough
to be your daughter!

674
01:00:03.704 --> 01:00:06.081
Ah Jin, are you all right?

675
01:00:06.748 --> 01:00:08.500
Can you hear me?

676
01:00:09.251 --> 01:00:10.544
Look at you.

677
01:00:13.255 --> 01:00:16.174
You son of a bitch!

678
01:00:52.586 --> 01:00:54.087
And in that wager

679
01:00:55.881 --> 01:00:57.841
God took her side.

680
01:01:19.321 --> 01:01:20.405
My dad...

681
01:01:23.200 --> 01:01:25.535
Please come and help my dad.

682
01:01:26.828 --> 01:01:30.165
He's bleeding so much.

683
01:01:31.666 --> 01:01:33.210
My dad...

684
01:01:33.835 --> 01:01:35.921
It's 13 Nojeong-dong, Nojeong-gu.

685
01:01:37.172 --> 01:01:38.381
The rooftop house.

686
01:01:39.758 --> 01:01:42.302
Please save my dad's life.

687
01:01:46.556 --> 01:01:48.308
Please hurry.

688
01:02:12.332 --> 01:02:18.088
And so, she offered up a sacrifice
and broke free from her shackles.

689
01:03:14.144 --> 01:03:18.565
DEAR X

690
01:05:38.663 --> 01:05:40.665
Subtitles by Ho Young Yun

